WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.526
AI is drinking India's water.

00:00:02.781 --> 00:00:04.923
But can it even see where that water goes?

00:00:06.023 --> 00:00:10.828
Code builds a landscape and makes it rain, so it knows every answer before it asks.

00:00:11.028 --> 00:00:14.735
Then it paints each scene three ways: satellite, map and thermal.

00:00:15.835 --> 00:00:19.864
Every scene has a twin. One tiny change, and the answer flips.

00:00:20.964 --> 00:00:25.423
A separate library re-checks every answer. And we published our own audit.

00:00:26.523 --> 00:00:28.794
Open models? Guessing.

00:00:28.951 --> 00:00:32.762
Gemini Flash-Lite reads the map. Hide it, and it's guessing again.

00:00:32.921 --> 00:00:36.774
Gemini 3.5 Flash? Seventy-seven percent.

00:00:37.874 --> 00:00:39.294
Then the twins catch it.

00:00:39.447 --> 00:00:43.908
Cool the water, and it gives the exact same answer. Two false heat alarms.

00:00:44.115 --> 00:00:46.616
Both halves right in just six of nineteen pairs.

00:00:47.716 --> 00:00:51.986
Got a model? Score it on the public leaderboard, right in your browser.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:57.910
Over five thousand seven hundred tasks. A live demo. Everything open.

00:00:58.126 --> 00:01:02.268
Before we trust AI with India's water, it should have to pass this test.
